{
  "summary": "Removes the default constructor and `Init()` method from `PrecomputedTransactionData`, enforcing that transaction data and any spent outputs are provided at construction time. Validation and test paths that require deferred evaluation switch to `std::optional<PrecomputedTransactionData>`, emplacing the object only after a script-cache miss. The change also avoids allocating unused txdata storage during `ConnectBlock()` when assumevalid skips script verification, and eliminates an unintended copy of caller-supplied txdata in the experimental bitcoinkernel C verification API.",
  "problem": "`PrecomputedTransactionData` could exist without transaction data and be reinitialized via `Init()`. Its old guard only checked `m_spent_outputs_ready`, leaving BIP143 sighash caches vulnerable to partial overwrite if `Init()` were called again. Additionally, ternary expression typing caused the kernel C verification API to copy caller txdata on every verification call, and `ConnectBlock()` allocated vector elements for transactions even when assumevalid skipped script checks.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The old Init() guard only checked m_spent_outputs_ready, which remained false after initialization without spent outputs even when the BIP143 prevout, sequence, and output hashes were already cached.'",
    "Commit d432b35312 links a Compiler Explorer reproducer (https://godbolt.org/z/PzcKGW9da) demonstrating the unintended copy in GCC 15.2 before the fix and none after."
  ],
